 deductive reasoning in social research?","b":"Testing a theory by deriving hypotheses and examining evidence","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b9","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper1","PPP::Topic::theory-and-methods","PPP::Class::content"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Key content::Paper 1: Education with theory and methods::Theory and methods::4.1.3 (9) The relationship between theory and methods"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-content:b2d93235dffa9e1845a9","f":"Which approach typically uses deduction to test hypotheses?","b":"Positivism","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b9","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper1","PPP::Topic::theory-and-methods","PPP::Class::content"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Key content::Paper 1: Education with theory and methods::Theory and methods::4.1.3 (9) The relationship between theory and methods"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-content:9044aa63a2c6d90b8006","f":"Which approach commonly uses induction to build interpretations?","b":"Interpretivism","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b9","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper1","PPP::Topic::theory-and-methods","PPP::Class::content"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Key content::Paper 1: Education with theory and methods::Theory and methods::4.1.3 (9) The relationship between theory and methods"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-content:9dad9984c198832537a4","f":"What is grounded theory designed to do?","b":"Generate theory systematically from qualitative data","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b9","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper1","PPP::Topic::theory-and-methods","PPP::Class::content"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Key content::Paper 1: Education with theory and methods::Theory and methods::4.1.3 (9) The relationship between theory and methods"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-content:ed02e145750ec6fee67c","f":"What did Weber mean by value relevance in research?","b":"Values influence which topics researchers choose","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b10",